Ah, those five little letters, Y A F A P.

I've been playing this game for years, &c, &c.  Still hard to believe
that the world is, at last, safe from Moloch. Unfortunately, this game
lasted a number of months, and I'm too impatient to take notes. Maybe
now that I've been to the Immortals' Bar I'll be more journalistically
savvy next time round.

This was in Slash'Em 0.0.7E6F1, ultimately. The big scare came when I
was going back to get the Key of Law, and I disarmed an Aleax and the
dungeon crashed around me. Ali Harow set me straight, though, and I
continued on to glory.
I also fell in some lava (that red is really hard to see on my
monitor) and zapped my wand of cold. Nothing happens. What do you
know, it's my only one! Odin liked me, though. Whew.

I only found one ?oGenocide, and I used it for Nurses. If I'd found
another it would have gone to Disenchanters, no question. Got to the
point where I couldn't throw my Mjollnir anymore!

The only Rider I met was Famine, and I filled him before he had a
chance to attack. I was a little over-prepared, perhaps, as the final
levels didn't seem very difficult. Frightening, yes, but not too hard.
Rodney only doubled up once, and really the worst thing he ever did
was to dump me in a pool of water, which cost me a number of scrolls.
I found Odin's alter on the first try, and never had to bother with
Death or Taxes. I thought about exploring, but then I thought about
YAFAP. I tried to come up with some clever thing to do, but then I
thought that ascending for the first time was pretty durn clever. (:
Next time I'll do it Blind, or Standing on One Leg, or something.

